I go into the museum's small cafeteria.
I order a cutting chai there.
I take this cup of tea and sit near the window.
Outside in the courtyard, the rain is falling very heavily.
I look at that rain and think.
Five months ago, Mumbai was so dry!
A woman is sitting at the next table.
She looks at the window and says to me.
"This rain is very beautiful, isn't it?"
I smile and nod.
"Yes, it is very beautiful," I tell her.
She drinks her tea and says again.
"But these days this weather changes very quickly."
I agree with her.
"Yes, a little while ago there was bright sunshine outside."
She smiles and looks outside again.
I drink my hot chai slowly.
This quiet moment feels very nice.
